[{"body":"Found while fixing #138 in the UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING builder\n(culturebotai-claw). Measured over `data/ingredients/mapped/*.yaml` on\n2026-09-06; numbers, not recollection.\n\n## Measurement\n\n```\nmapped records                                   2,678\ncarrying kg_microbe_node_id                        376\nkg_microbe_node_id ≠ identifier                     51\n  same prefix (a contradictory \"corrected\" column)  29   ← 2,400 occurrences\n  cross prefix                                      22\n```\n\nThe same-prefix 29, by occurrences:\n\n| record | identifier | kg_microbe_node_id | occ |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| `Coso4_X_7_H2o` | `CHEBI:91244` (heptahydrate) | `CHEBI:53470` (anhydrous) | 828 |\n| `Edta` | `CHEBI:4735` (free acid) | `CHEBI:64755` (EDTA(2−)) | 569 |\n| `Na2hpo4_X_2_H2o` | `CHEBI:91258` | `CHEBI:34683` | 304 |\n| `Hepes` | `CHEBI:42334` | `CHEBI:46756` | 251 |\n| `Thiamine` | `CHEBI:18385` | `CHEBI:26948` | 159 |\n| `Na2hpo4_X_12_H2o` | `CHEBI:91259` | `CHEBI:34683` | 159 |\n| `Fructose` | `CHEBI:28757` | `CHEBI:28645` | 87 |\n| `Thiamine_pyrophosphate` | `CHEBI:9532` | `CHEBI:18290` | 26 |\n\nEvery one is a MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 correction — hydration state, free acid\nvs anion, specific vs generic — applied to `identifier` while\n`kg_microbe_node_id` stayed on the id it superseded. The record asserts two\nidentities at once.\n\n## Why it is #138's problem one column over\n\n`kg_microbe_node_id` flows verbatim into `UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING.tsv`, and\nkg-microbe reads it. Two consequences, both already live:\n\n1. **Its corrected-first ranker prefers the stale value.** kg-microbe#723 added\n   `corrected_column_primary([kg_node_id, mim_id, chebi_id, culturemech_term,\n   cas])` to report divergences — `kg_node_id` first. For these 29 rows that\n   path grounds to the superseded id and reports MIM's actual `identifier` as\n   the disagreement. The \"corrected\" column is the one that is wrong.\n2. **It masks the #138 mechanism in analysis.** Any TSV-level check that treats\n   `mim_id`/`kg_microbe_node_id` as \"MIM's answer\" sees them disagree and cannot\n   tell which is stale. It fooled mine: I under-counted #138's blast radius by 5\n   rows (HEPES, TPP, CMC…) until I compared against `identifier` alone.\n\nThe builder fix for #138 (claw PR, in flight) deliberately keys precedence on\n`mim_id` = `identifier`, so the published `chebi_id`/`culturemech_term_id` are\nnow right for these rows — but `kg_microbe_node_id` still ships the\ncontradiction, because the builder copies the record field and correcting\nrecord data is not a builder's job.\n\n## What I did not do\n\nNot touched in the #138 PR: this is record curation, 29 records, and each\ncorrection should append a `curation_history` event. Nor did I infer which\nside is right by rule — every case I looked at favours `identifier`, and the\n§3 pattern says the same, but that is what a curation pass is for.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nA one-off pass that, for records where `kg_microbe_node_id` and `identifier`\nshare a prefix and differ, sets `kg_microbe_node_id = identifier` with a\nhistory event citing this issue — plus a `qc-duplicate-ids`-style invariant so\na future §3 correction to `identifier` cannot leave the sibling field behind\nagain. The 22 cross-prefix cases (e.g. a CHEBI identifier with a FOODON node\nid) may be legitimate dual-classification and want a look, not a rule.","number":554,"state":"closed","title":"29 records publish a kg_microbe_node_id that contradicts their own identifier (2,400 occurrences) — the corrected-first ranker would pick the stale one","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/554"},{"body":"## Problem\n\nThe CultureMech-to-MIM import loses the grouping that says which recipes contain\nan ingredient, and it can undercount `media_count`.\n\nCultureMech's aggregator initially records an occurrence with medium name,\ncategory, file path, and ingredient position. Its exported aggregate then keeps\nonly the first 50 occurrence examples:\n\n```python\n'media_occurrences': data['media_occurrences'][:50]\n```\n\nMIM imports that sample as:\n\n```python\n'media_count': len(ingredient.get('media_occurrences', []))\n```\n\nTherefore `media_count` is capped at 50 for high-frequency ingredients and is a\ncount of retained occurrence examples, not necessarily unique media. MIM then\ndiscards the occurrence list, so the source recipe memberships cannot be\nreconstructed.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `../CultureMech/scripts/aggregate_mapped_ingredients.py:156-173,242-249`\n- `scripts/import_from_culturemech.py:107-145,148-177`\n- `src/mediaingredientmech/schema/mediaingredientmech.yaml:468-496`\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define a lossless ingredient-to-recipe occurrence artifact keyed by a MIM\n  ingredient identity and stable CultureMech medium ID.\n- Prefer a generated sidecar edge table if embedding every membership would\n  bloat curated ingredient YAML.\n- Preserve useful occurrence provenance such as source path/category and\n  ingredient position where available.\n- Derive `media_count` from unique recipe IDs and check `total_occurrences`\n  against the full edge population.\n- Stop deriving either value from a capped example list.\n- Add orphan, duplicate-edge, and count-consistency validation.\n- Publish a machine-readable artifact that answers “which CultureMech recipes\n  use this ingredient?” without copying full recipe bodies into MIM.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A fresh import preserves every source ingredient-to-recipe membership.\n- [ ] `media_count` is derived from unique stable recipe IDs and is not capped at\n      50.\n- [ ] `total_occurrences` has a documented definition and is reproducible from\n      the imported occurrence data.\n- [ ] Duplicate memberships and unknown recipe IDs are rejected or reported.\n- [ ] Re-running the import is deterministic and does not create duplicate edges.\n- [ ] A published artifact supports recipe-membership lookup by MIM ingredient.\n- [ ] Tests include an ingredient occurring in more than 50 recipes.\n\n## Dependencies and related work\n\n- Depends on the stable CultureMech recipe-reference contract in #447.\n- Distinct from closed #196, which added source-scoped prevalence for non-media\n  sources; this issue concerns actual CultureMech recipe memberships.\n","number":449,"state":"open","title":"CultureMech import derives media_count from a capped example list and drops recipe memberships","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/449"},{"body":"Found by cross-checking MIM against **CultureBotAI/CultureMech#272**, which independently regrounds the same labels — and is right where MIM is wrong.\n\nThis is the identity half of #321, still open for these seven. Each names a hydrate, sits on an anhydrous or generic ChEBI term, and ChEBI **has** the specific hydrate term, so `MAPPING_SEMANTICS` §3 **step 1** applies and nothing needs minting:\n\n| record | currently on | should be |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Chromium(III) Chloride Hexahydrate` | `CHEBI:53351` chromium(3+) trichloride | `CHEBI:53442` …hexahydrate |\n| `CoSO4 x 7 H2O` | `CHEBI:53470` cobalt(2+) sulfate | `CHEBI:91244` …heptahydrate |\n| `FeSO4 x 7H2O` | `CHEBI:75832` iron(2+) sulfate **(anhydrous)** | `CHEBI:75836` …heptahydrate |\n| `MgSO4·7H2O` | `CHEBI:32599` magnesium sulfate | `CHEBI:31795` …heptahydrate |\n| `MnSO4 x 1 H2O` | `CHEBI:86360` manganese(II) sulfate | `CHEBI:86364` …monohydrate |\n| `Na2SeO3·5H2O` | `CHEBI:48843` disodium selenite | `CHEBI:131361` …pentahydrate |\n| `NiSO4 x 7 H2O` | `CHEBI:53001` nickel sulfate | `CHEBI:53504` …heptahydrate |\n\n`FeSO4 x 7H2O` is the sharpest: its term is explicitly labelled **\"(anhydrous)\"** while the record's own label says 7 H2O.\n\n## Two complications, both worth settling in the same pass\n\n**1. Some targets are already held.** `CHEBI:75836` is held by `FeSO4 x 7 H2O` (note the space — a near-duplicate of `FeSO4 x 7H2O`, and one of the ten pairs recorded on #334). So this is a promotion for some and a **merge** for others; `fix_hydrate_collapse.py` already handles both shapes and distinguishes them by whether the target identifier is taken.\n\n**2. #342 decided hydrate→anhydrous is `closeMatch`.** That decision was about records whose hydrate has *no* ChEBI term. These seven do have one, so they move to `EXACT_MATCH` on the specific term and leave the closeMatch question behind entirely — worth stating explicitly so the two decisions are not read as conflicting.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSurfaced by diffing CultureMech#272's chosen `term.id` against MIM's answer for every name it changes: 27 changed, 11 agree with MIM, **16 disagree**. On the hydrate subset the disagreement is MIM's fault, and these 7 are it. (The remaining disagreements are covered by CultureBotAI/CultureMech#260 and by one genuine defect in #272 flagged there.)","number":374,"state":"closed","title":"7 hydrate records sit on the anhydrous term while ChEBI has the specific hydrate","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/374"},{"body":"While implementing a retraction pass in kg-microbe for the 16 superseded groundings flagged in `culturebotai-claw` `workspace/reports/propagation_2026-07-19.md`, we found that **3 of the 16 are not just re-seeding phantoms** — kg-microbe's `load_culturebotai_reviewed` **actively re-asserts them every run** from the current `UNIFIED_INGREDIENT_MAPPING.tsv`, because a corrected grounding was written to `kg_microbe_node_id` / `mim_id` while the **superseded value was left in a higher-precedence column** (`chebi_id` / `culturemech_term_id`).\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe kg-microbe loader selects the primary CURIE with:\n\n```\nbest_primary([chebi_id, culturemech_term_id, mim_id, kg_microbe_node_id, cas_rn])\n```\n\nWithin one prefix (e.g. all `CHEBI:`) the rank is equal, so the **first candidate in that list wins** — `chebi_id` outranks `kg_microbe_node_id` / `mim_id`. When a correction updates `kg_microbe_node_id` / `mim_id` but leaves the old id in `chebi_id` (or `culturemech_term_id`), the consumer grounds to the **stale** value and demotes the correction to a mere xref.\n\n## The 3 cases (current file)\n\n| ingredient(s) | consumer picks (stale) | intended (in kg_node/mim) | stale column(s) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 4-Aminobenzoic acid, PABA, Para-aminobenzoic acid | `CHEBI:194474` (4-ammoniobenzoate) | `CHEBI:30753` (4-aminobenzoic acid) | `chebi_id`, `culturemech_term_id` |\n| Cobalamine | `CHEBI:30411` (cobalamin) | `CHEBI:28911` (Cobalamine) | `chebi_id`, `culturemech_term_id` |\n| Infusion from Potatoes | `FOODON:03316428` (**Peptone**) | — (Peptone is wrong for a potato infusion) | `culturemech_term_id` |\n\nNotes:\n- For the PABA *variant* rows (`p-Amino Benzoic Acid`, `p-amino benzoic acid`; status `CHEBI_NO_MIM`), `kg_microbe_node_id` / `mim_id` are **empty** and only `chebi_id` / `culturemech_term_id = CHEBI:194474` are set — so those rows assert *only* the stale id. The correction (`CHEBI:30753`) exists only on the canonical `4-Aminobenzoic acid` row.\n- The ~80 peptone/tryptone/casein rows also historically grounded to `FOODON:03316428` are **already fixed** (`MICRO:0000178` peptone, `MICRO:0000182` tryptone, `MICRO:0000180` proteose peptone, `FOODON:03315719` casein hydrolysate, …). `FOODON:03316428` (\"Peptone\") now survives only through the single mis-annotated \"Infusion from Potatoes\" row.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nWhen a grounding is corrected, also **clear or update the superseded value in `chebi_id` and `culturemech_term_id`** (and propagate the correction to all name-variant rows), so each row has a single consistent source of truth. Otherwise the stale column silently outranks the correction in any consumer that ranks id columns by position. For \"Infusion from Potatoes\", the `culturemech_term_id = FOODON:03316428` (\"Peptone\") looks like a mis-annotation to fix or drop.\n\n## kg-microbe side (context, no action needed here)\n\nkg-microbe now runs a retraction pass that drops these every consolidation, and the correct groundings are independently present, so the published graph is clean. We deliberately did **not** reorder the consumer's column precedence (`kg_microbe_node_id`-first), because that would shift ~35 unrelated groundings (Fructose, Cholesterol, Casein, …) that need separate curation review. This issue is only so the root cause is fixed in the source data.\n\n_Reported from KG-Microbe consolidation tooling._\n","number":138,"state":"closed","title":"Stale chebi_id/culturemech_term_id columns outrank corrected kg_microbe_node_id/mim_id (3 superseded groundings re-asserted)","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/138"}]
